urceKey":"run","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"27"},"destinationKey":"b","guid":"79a0f97e-cc29-491c-a161-2df97bc1ca31","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"27"},"sourceKey":"product","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"29"},"destinationKey":"a","guid":"d39e354a-4ba3-400c-a70d-c8eee876327c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"25"},"sourceKey":"kept","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"29"},"destinationKey":"b","guid":"cba57f36-2227-4251-a2c5-5879c0eb77ba","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"29"},"sourceKey":"product","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"31"},"destinationKey":"number","guid":"e14e0782-086e-4cbb-95a3-6278672c9d84","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"position":{"xMin":-40.0,"yMin":-80.0,"xMax":2460.0,"yMax":540.0},"label":"How rough a tide race is","comment":"Its own roughness, by how hard the stream runs (nothing at slack water). A third of that at the least; more with the wind against the stream (from 2 m/s, all of it at 10); more again in a hard wind (from 8 to 16); a fifth over at the most.","color":{"r":0.32,"g":0.55,"b":0.32,"a":1.0},"guid":"3da51f23-a501-4a73-af80-752a6ed36b35","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-20.0,"yMin":300.0,"xMax":460.0,"yMax":450.0},"title":"Where the numbers come from","body":"The water''s own roughness is in Game/Data/rough_waters_793.json. How hard the stream runs is the tide model''s, against its own hardest there in a fortnight. The shares on the nodes (0.35, 0.65, 0.2; 2 to 10, 8 to 16; 1.2) are this rule''s own: change them here.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"d83a7b29-2868-4143-ab9e-77c65350d654","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"}],"$version":"A"}}'
